st used in the original crisis it's  basically all about sampling the depth  of other pixels around an area and from  that it calculates the shadow H Bao or  horizon based I mean occlusion is better  and generates higher-quality SSAO by  increasing the number of samples per  pixel but as a result it's a tad more  demanding on your hardware it samples  the environment at half resolution  though to lessen the power required and  what about H Dao you ask well honestly I  don't know I'm not a member of the  highland dancers Association of Ontario  and those guys have the best SEO  oh you mean High Definition ambient  occlusion oh yes well that's broadly  similar to H Bao except that it's AMD's  own version of ambient occlusion poof  well that's the complicate one other way  so let's move on to an easy one with fov  not POV instantly as some YouTube  comments on my previous video thoughts  POV eh  I wonder where you heard that one before  I mean obviously I am no idea what that  is I've never heard of it never what is  it price of vegetables fov or field of  view on the other hand is the extent of  the observable game world that is seen  on the display at any given moment the  wider the angle the more you see so does  this hit your pcs performance well it  shouldn't much if anything at all sure  there might be more objects on screen at  a wider angle but they're also slightly  further away so depending on how the  game loads and textures and should  balance out okay next up is DOF or depth  of field right now hold your hand up in  front of your face like this  and focus on your hands right it should  be all sharp and looking great but  everything behind it including this  monitor screen should be all blurry and  out of focus  that's because of depth of field  technically it means the distance  between the nearest and farthest objects  in a scene that both appear acceptable  sharp or InFocus now as a video producer  I work with depth of field every day  doing so lets you 